% A shorthand decoration at the end of a line of music decorates nothing,
% which is an error.  parsenote() (parseabc.c) took the '\0' that ends the
% line for a decoration: it wrote past the end of its array of decorations
% and went on reading after the end of the line.  Like the other overflow
% guards, the value of this sample is under the sanitizer build.
X:1
T:Shorthand decoration at the end of a line
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
C D E F |H
G A B c |]
